* Hermetic ngspice init for sim/tank-characterization.
*
* run_pvt_sweep.sh copies this file into the scratch directory it runs
* ngspice from, so a run does NOT depend on whether $HOME/.spiceinit exists
* (the PDK ships libs.tech/ngspice/install.py, which symlinks one into $HOME;
* a cold-start checkout on a machine where that was never run must still
* reproduce the committed numbers).
*
* ngbehavior=hsa is the compatibility mode the PDK own .spiceinit sets, and
* is what its model libraries are written against. For the passive models
* this experiment exercises the mode is not actually load-bearing -- the
* extracted C, Q and SRF were verified bit-identical with the mode off --
* but it is set anyway so this tree matches the PDK documented ngspice
* setup rather than quietly diverging from it.
set ngbehavior=hsa
